Date: Sun, 8 Nov 2026 15:03:12 +0900
Subject: [PATCH 419/423] Design check: whether parts touch, face by face; pins
 in holes by a sweep along x

A cart of STEP casters and hundreds of screws spent 98 s in distToShape
between whole solids (a quarter of a second each) and 33 s comparing every
round face with every other (4 million box tests). Now each shape's solids,
faces and round faces are prepared once with their boxes; only faces whose
boxes come within the distance are measured, and the pairs of boxes are
found by sorting along x. Two compounds of 400 screws: 3.8 s to 0.09 s.
The issues found are the same.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
